<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  :feature:antivirus declares exactly one permission, and only because code in THIS module calls the
  API behind it: `AntivirusScanRoute` reads `ConnectivityManager` to report the network gate upward
  as `GateStateReported(isOnline = …)` (docs/screens/15-antivirus.md §1.3 — platform truth lives in
  the composable, MVI §4). `ConnectivityManager.getNetworkCapabilities` throws a SecurityException
  without it.

  The same rule the :data manifest states applies here: only what code in this module actually calls.
  Nothing else is declared on another cluster's or another decision's behalf.

  Deliberately NOT here:
    * The storage read permissions — declared by :data, beside MediaStoreQuery, which is the code
      that uses them. This module only *asks* for them through an ActivityResultContract.
    * MANAGE_EXTERNAL_STORAGE — never assumed grantable (system-architecture.md §8.1, owner
      decision). The scan degrades to ScanCoverage.InstalledAppsOnly and SAYS SO instead.
    * QUERY_ALL_PACKAGES — this module enumerates no packages. The result rows' icons come from
      AppIconLoader and fall back when a package is not visible; a permission a store listing has to
      justify is not declared to improve an icon.
    * REQUEST_DELETE_PACKAGES — the uninstall goes through Intent.ACTION_DELETE, which is the system
      dialog and needs no permission. ACTION_UNINSTALL_PACKAGE, which would, is not used.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE" />

</manifest>
